desc.chomper_11=__UNTRANSLATED__latch onto your head and bite
desc.chomper_12=__UNTRANSLATED__it off, literally.
desc.bug_6=__UNTRANSLATED__ These critters occasionally dig up
desc.bug_7=__UNTRANSLATED__Infusion Cores, and will do it faster
desc.bug_8=__UNTRANSLATED__if given Lustrian Crystals and it will
desc.bug_9=__UNTRANSLATED__pacify them for the time being, also
desc.bug_10=__UNTRANSLATED__they will try to attack you while
desc.bug_11=__UNTRANSLATED__attempting to pacify them. They also
desc.bug_12=__UNTRANSLATED__drop a carapace and food upon being
desc.bug_13=__UNTRANSLATED__slain.
desc.stal_6=__UNTRANSLATED__Terrifying creatures that seem to
desc.stal_7=__UNTRANSLATED__have some relations to Endermen.
desc.stal_8=__UNTRANSLATED__They like to stalk there prey while
desc.stal_9=__UNTRANSLATED__slowly approaching. If they get close
desc.stal_10=__UNTRANSLATED__enough they will frantically attack
desc.stal_11=__UNTRANSLATED__there target. If you see them before
desc.stal_12=__UNTRANSLATED__they attack, they'll run back into
desc.stal_13=__UNTRANSLATED__the darkness only to disappear again.
title.end_fort_0=__UNTRANSLATED__The Ashed King's Fortress
desc.fort_0=__UNTRANSLATED__The mighty fortress that shrouds atop
desc.fort_1=__UNTRANSLATED__the Wastelands. Could what's up there
desc.fort_2=__UNTRANSLATED__be the cause of such treachery?
desc.fort_3=__UNTRANSLATED__Would it even be wise to go up there?
desc.fort_4=__UNTRANSLATED__It is recommended to have your absolute
desc.fort_5=__UNTRANSLATED__best gear when attempting this dungeon.
desc.fort_6=__UNTRANSLATED__Stock up on food, healing potions,
desc.fort_7=__UNTRANSLATED__anything to give you the needed boost
desc.fort_8=__UNTRANSLATED__traveller. It's time to end this.
title.ot_str_0=__UNTRANSLATED__Other Structures
desc.ot_0=__UNTRANSLATED__Theres many other structures that lie
desc.ot_1=__UNTRANSLATED__within the Ash Wastelands. Such as
desc.ot_2=__UNTRANSLATED__The Ashed Towers that can prove
desc.ot_3=__UNTRANSLATED__a pre-test to the actual Fortress.
desc.ot_4=__UNTRANSLATED__There are other structures such as
desc.ot_5=__UNTRANSLATED__Ashed Mines that are underground,
desc.ot_6=__UNTRANSLATED__and outposts out in the distance.
desc.ot_7=__UNTRANSLATED__Hunting for these ruins in the
desc.ot_8=__UNTRANSLATED__wastelands can prove beneficial.
title.knights_0=__UNTRANSLATED__The Fell Household
desc.knig_6=__UNTRANSLATED__Although not native to the end, the
desc.knig_7=__UNTRANSLATED__knights are far from what they once
desc.knig_8=__UNTRANSLATED__we're. These crazed power hungry
desc.knig_9=__UNTRANSLATED__fanatics invaded the End just to
desc.knig_10=__UNTRANSLATED__feel their love for war again.
desc.knig_11=__UNTRANSLATED__However, following using Lustrian
desc.knig_12=__UNTRANSLATED__Crystals they have seemed to lost
desc.knig_13=__UNTRANSLATED__there sentience and only seek more.
title.knights_1=__UNTRANSLATED__The Fell Household Cont.
desc.mage_0=__UNTRANSLATED__These knights have specializations,
desc.mage_1=__UNTRANSLATED__and have different methods of combat.
desc.mage_2=__UNTRANSLATED__Mages, cast spells, heal there allies,
desc.mage_3=__UNTRANSLATED__and can perform a ritual to turn on of
desc.mage_4=__UNTRANSLATED__there own into something stronger.
desc.mage_5=__UNTRANSLATED__Swordsmen are fast and barbaric in
desc.mage_6=__UNTRANSLATED__there style, closing the gap and
desc.mage_7=__UNTRANSLATED__releasing a flurry of attacks. While
desc.mage_8=__UNTRANSLATED__the shielder is slow but highly
desc.mage_9=__UNTRANSLATED__defensive. As tough as they seem to
desc.mage_10=__UNTRANSLATED__be removed. A timed parry can disable
desc.mage_11=__UNTRANSLATED__there shield for a short period of
desc.mage_12=__UNTRANSLATED__time allowing you to strike them.
desc.dd_helm_6=__UNTRANSLATED__The Dark armour set, this set only
desc.dd_helm_7=__UNTRANSLATED__contains it's helmet and chest
desc.dd_helm_8=__UNTRANSLATED__piece for the full bonus to take
desc.dd_helm_9=__UNTRANSLATED__effect. With the bonus being
desc.dd_helm_10=__UNTRANSLATED__immunity to the Red Rage
desc.dd_helm_11=__UNTRANSLATED__potion effect.
desc.dd_cont_6=__UNTRANSLATED__In other words, basically allowing
desc.dd_cont_7=__UNTRANSLATED__you to carry Lustrian Crystals, Chunks,
desc.dd_cont_8=__UNTRANSLATED__and the Lustrian sword and any attacks
desc.dd_cont_9=__UNTRANSLATED__that deliver the Red Rage.
desc.chad_6=__UNTRANSLATED__This beast of a warrior is created
desc.chad_7=__UNTRANSLATED__by Mages casting a curse on other
desc.chad_8=__UNTRANSLATED__Knights. They are very fast in there
desc.chad_9=__UNTRANSLATED__attacks, and will even try to block
desc.chad_10=__UNTRANSLATED__your melee attacks. Not many get to
desc.chad_11=__UNTRANSLATED__witness one of these warriors in
desc.chad_12=__UNTRANSLATED__action as you'll be lucky to leave
desc.chad_13=__UNTRANSLATED__alive.
desc.king_6=__UNTRANSLATED__The one to blame for this blasphemy.
desc.king_7=__UNTRANSLATED__He is the one kindling all together,
desc.king_8=__UNTRANSLATED__he alone was the power to break the
desc.king_9=__UNTRANSLATED__End. He must be stopped at all costs.
desc.king_10=__UNTRANSLATED__You may find him atop the main
desc.king_11=__UNTRANSLATED__fortress by using an Ashed Key on
desc.king_12=__UNTRANSLATED__the key block. As he unlocks your
desc.king_13=__UNTRANSLATED__full potential.
title.barrend_bogs.name=__UNTRANSLATED__The Barrend Bogs
